  "term": "ambivalent attachment",
  "definition": "Ambivalent attachment, described here as an anxiety-ambivalent attachment style, is a form of insecure attachment. In this source, higher levels of this style in mothers are linked with using food to manage emotions and with lower nutrition knowledge.",
